-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party models (NOT included in this repository)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Sosia can optionally use a local named-entity recognition model. The model files
are NOT distributed with Sosia: each user downloads them separately from the
original authors and accepts their licenses.

1. GLiNER multi PII v1 - urchade/gliner_multi_pii-v1
   https://huggingface.co/urchade/gliner_multi_pii-v1
   License: Apache License 2.0
   GLiNER: Zaratiana, Tomeh, Holat, Charnois, "GLiNER: Generalist Model for
   Named Entity Recognition using Bidirectional Transformer", NAACL 2024.
   Library: https://github.com/urchade/GLiNER (Apache License 2.0)

2. mDeBERTa-v3-base - microsoft/mdeberta-v3-base (tokenizer vocabulary and
   configuration, used by GLiNER as its backbone)
   https://huggingface.co/microsoft/mdeberta-v3-base
   License: MIT License, Copyright (c) Microsoft Corporation

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party data included in sosia/dizionari/ (extracts, since 0.6.0)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The files below are EXTRACTS (names only, reformatted and filtered) rebuilt by
scripts/build_dictionaries.py from the original files, whose SHA-256 are listed in
sosia/dizionari/FONTI.json. The original files are not distributed.

1. istat_comuni.txt, istat_localita.txt
   Source: Istat - Istituto nazionale di statistica, "Elenco dei comuni italiani"
   (21/02/2026) and "Basi territoriali 2021 - Localita puntuali".
   License: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0).
   Changes: only names, province codes and cadastral codes kept; inhabited
   centres and nuclei only; names equal to a municipality removed.

2. osn_luoghi_gb.txt, osn_vie_gb.txt
   Contains OS data (c) Crown copyright and database right 2026 (OS Open Names,
   October 2026). Licensed under the Open Government Licence v3.0.
   Changes: only settlement names with county, and names of roads without a
   street-type suffix, kept.

3. ons_nomi_uk.txt
   Source: Office for National Statistics, "Baby names in England and Wales:
   1996 to 2025". Contains public sector information licensed under the Open
   Government Licence v3.0. Changes: names with at least 100 births in total,
   with prevailing sex.

4. census_cognomi_us.txt
   Source: U.S. Census Bureau, 2010 Census surnames (File B). Public domain
   (work of the U.S. federal government). Changes: surnames with at least 200
   occurrences, title case.

5. wikidata_nomi_it.txt, wikidata_cognomi_it.txt
   Source: Wikidata (query of 28/10/2026), released under CC0 1.0.

